<title>RUSSIA: Gazprom rises to 2,951.48 rbls.</title>
<headline>Gazprom rises to 2,951.48 rbls.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A stake of 10 million shares in Russian natural gas monopoly RAO Gazprom sold at auction on Friday at an average 2,951.48 roubles ($0.545) a share, up from 2,946.93 roubles at the previous auction on September 30, the Federal Securities Corporation (FFK) said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction:</p>
<p>						 Oct 4	  Sept 30</p>
<p>    Total shares traded		 10 million	   10 million</p>
<p>    as pct of capital		    0.042	    0.042</p>
<p>    Starting price (roubles)	   2,799	    2,794</p>
<p>    Minimum price			  2,857	    2,865</p>
<p>    Maximum price			  3,030	    3,020</p>
<p>    Average price			  2,951.48	 2,946.93</p>
<p>    Number of lots			    40		n/a</p>
<p>    Total volume traded (mln rbls)  29,514.75	   n/a</p>
<p>The FFK said that since auctions began in March, 189.75 million shares, equivalent to 0.80 percent of the capital, had changed hands.</p>
<p>Prices have risen from an average 406.6 roubles a shares at the first auction on March 6.</p>
<p>Gazprom is Russia's biggest company by market capitalisation but its 23.6 billion shares are highly illiquid, because of company restrictions on selling them.</p>
<p>The company has organised the auctions to create an orderly market in its paper.</p>
<p>Gazprom closed at $0.335 on the Russian Trading System, up from $0.325 on Thursday.</p>
<p>The company plans an international placement of depositary receipts in early October.</p>
<p>Further auctions will be held on October 11, 21 and 25, and November 1 and 10.</p>
<p>($=5,415 roubles)</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
